# The tests generate a CA, a server certificate and a server key into pytest's tmp dir every
# session, and the anchor manifest they write is derived from them. None of it is evidence: a
# committed throwaway key would look like a pin, and a pin is exactly the thing this repository
# must never gain by accident.
#
# `tests/fixtures/*` rather than `tests/fixtures/` so the files below can be re-included: they are not
# generated output but captured evidence - the real keys and real STHs of two production logs, which the
# pinning tests need in order to refuse a fake rather than only another fake, and the entry corpus the entry
# and CA-graph tests are measured on. `entry-corpus.json` was written by `tools/corpus.py`, and it is still
# evidence rather than build output: its prefix is bound to a signed tree head by a consistency proof, so it
# cannot be regenerated at will and a fresh clone must carry the bytes it was verified against. Anything a
# test creates at runtime stays ignored.
#
# `midwindow-corpus.json` earns its place the same way: 64 entries from the middle of Google's Xenon2027h1,
# each proved into that tree by its own audit path against the head captured beside it. The log has grown
# since, so a later run takes a different head at a different midpoint and cannot reproduce these bytes; a
# fresh clone has to carry the ones the proofs were checked against.
tests/fixtures/*
!tests/fixtures/log-pins.toml
!tests/fixtures/production-sth.json
!tests/fixtures/entry-corpus.json
!tests/fixtures/midwindow-corpus.json
